<div class="desktop x5dh21z"><div class="site-header-slot header-slot" data-pagefind-ignore><Header /></div><section class="hero xqwgqpu"><div class="hero-content xceripq"><div class="hero-copy xrufbgf"><div class="product-eyebrow xddcj0k fb"><svg class="xqfhqb3 icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(9.75 3)"></path><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 15.75)"></path><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(15.75 15.75)"></path><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(9.75 3)"></path><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 15.75)"></path><path d="M 0.75 4.5 C 0.336 4.5 0 4.164 0 3.75 L 0 0.75 C 0 0.336 0.336 0 0.75 0 L 3.75 0 C 4.164 0 4.5 0.336 4.5 0.75 L 4.5 3.75 C 4.5 4.164 4.164 4.5 3.75 4.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(15.75 15.75)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 0 3.75" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(12 7.5)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 0 4.5" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(18 11.25)"></path><path d="M 0 4.5 L 0 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(6 11.25)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 19.5 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(2.25 11.25)"></path></svg><p class="xffd8kr">AI data center optics</p></div><h1 class="xc7tr6j">Optical Transceivers for AI Clusters, 400G to 1.6T</h1><p class="xuayj2b">OSFP and QSFP-DD modules from 1.6T down to 1G, low-loss MPO, MTP and LC patch cords, and InfiniBand and Ethernet switches, supplied together for GPU clusters from H100 to GB300. Sourced from a top-tier optical module maker, tested for compatibility and quoted within 24 hours.</p><p class="xuayj2b hero-links">For the passive fiber behind the modules, see <a href="/data-center-fiber-cabling" class="text-link">data center fiber cabling</a>.</p><div class="hero-buttons xbf6anw"><a class="request-a-quote-button xi42qpw" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xvkflym">Request a Quote</p><svg class="xquoydi icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 9.75 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 12)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path></svg></a><a class="see-all-fibre-cables-button xaybavg fb" href="#reference-design"><p class="xzinndr">See the reference design</p></a><a class="x95svpw fb" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xzinndr">Talk to a Specifier</p></a></div></div><SpecPanel title={"AI cluster optics, supplied together"} chips={["1.6T, 800G and 400G","OSFP and QSFP-DD","200G down to 1G","Low-loss MPO and LC"]} note={"Need a different module or cord length? Send the part list and we will match it."} render="VC-106" alt="Optical transceiver range from SFP to OSFP" /></div><div class="trust-stats xmtn5ca"><div class="xe1af3r"><p class="x8h4uaa">100+</p><p class="xbgwdly">Regions</p></div><div class="xe1af3r"><p class="x8h4uaa">99.9%</p><p class="xbgwdly">Uptime</p></div><div class="xe1af3r"><p class="x8h4uaa">25,000+</p><p class="xbgwdly">Clients</p></div><div class="xe1af3r"><p class="x8h4uaa">24/7</p><p class="xbgwdly">Support</p></div></div></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="what-it-is xzpblpc"><div class="section-introduction xpfskxn"><h2 class="xhz5zt5">What it is</h2><p class="xuvmvsv">In an AI cluster the fiber is passive. The transceiver is where light becomes data, and every GPU server, leaf and spine port needs one matched to its speed, form factor and reach, with a patch cord matched to the module. A 32-server B300 cluster runs 1.6T between switches, 800G to every GPU network card, 400G and 200G on the Ethernet side and 25G down to 1G for management. We supply the whole set, so the optics, cords and switches arrive as one order.</p></div><div class="specification-table xcqzusx fb"><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Speeds</p><p class="xcclquv">1.6T, 800G, 400G, 200G, 100G, 25G, 10G and 1G</p></div><div class="strength-member-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Form factors</p><p class="xcclquv">OSFP and QSFP-DD for 400G to 1.6T</p></div><div class="fibre-type-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Fabrics</p><p class="xcclquv">InfiniBand and Ethernet, including RoCEv2 GPU backends</p></div><div class="fibre-counts-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Clusters supplied</p><p class="xcclquv">H100, H200, B300 and GB300</p></div><div class="sheath-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Patch cords</p><p class="xcclquv">MPO, MTP and LC, low insertion loss, custom lengths</p></div><div class="deployment-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Switches</p><p class="xcclquv">InfiniBand and Ethernet, from the original vendors</p></div><div class="standards-row xr2tetp"><p class="xbslay4">Quality</p><p class="xcclquv">Built to MSA and original-vendor specifications, full warranty service</p></div></div></section><section class="fibre-count-range xqjs4fo"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">Every speed in the cluster</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">From the 1.6T spine links down to the 1G out-of-band management ports, one supplier covers every port in the hall.</p><div class="count-rail xhrktuh"><div class="12f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">1G</p></div><div class="24f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">10G</p></div><div class="48f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">25G</p></div><div class="96f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">100G</p></div><div class="144f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">200G</p></div><div class="288f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">400G</p></div><div class="576f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">800G</p></div><div class="864f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">1.6T</p></div></div></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="trx-ref" id="reference-design"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">Where each module sits</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">Our reference design for 32 NVIDIA B300 HGX servers: an InfiniBand compute fabric, with Ethernet for north-south traffic and management.</p><figure class="trx-figure"><a href="/assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-2400.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-1200.webp 1200w, /assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-2400.webp 2400w" sizes="(max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, 1100px"/><img src="/assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-1200.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-1200.jpg 1200w, /assets/img/ai-cluster-reference-topology-2400.jpg 2400w" sizes="(max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, 1100px" width="2400" height="1880" alt="AI cluster network diagram: 32 B300 HGX servers on a 1.6T and 800G InfiniBand fabric, with 400G, 100G, 25G, 10G and 1G Ethernet for north-south traffic and management" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></a><figcaption>Reference topology for illustration. Port counts, optics and cabling vary by deployment. Tap to open full size.</figcaption></figure><dl class="trx-speeds"><div><dt>1.6T</dt><dd>InfiniBand leaf to spine, between QM3400 switches</dd></div><div><dt>800G</dt><dd>Leaf to every GPU server, eight ConnectX-8 network cards per server</dd></div><div><dt>400G</dt><dd>North-south Ethernet switching and InfiniBand fabric management (UFM)</dd></div><div><dt>400G to 2x 200G</dt><dd>Breakout to the BlueField-3 DPUs in each server</dd></div><div><dt>100G</dt><dd>Ethernet core to the management switches</dd></div><div><dt>25G</dt><dd>Management servers, dual-homed to both switches</dd></div><div><dt>10G and 1G</dt><dd>Firewalls, the internet edge and BMC out-of-band</dd></div></dl></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="trx-deploy"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">Clusters we have supplied</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">Optics, patch cords and switches for AI data halls in the US, Thailand and Taiwan, from H100 to GB300.</p><ul><li><p class="trx-where">Denver, USA · 2025</p><h3>H100 data hall</h3><p>High-volume 400G and 800G modules with low-loss patch cords. 100% of links passed on-site link and interoperability tests.</p></li><li><p class="trx-where">Denver, USA · 2025</p><h3>H200 data hall</h3><p>800G and 400G modules, InfiniBand switches for a non-blocking fabric, low-loss patch cords, and test and inspection equipment.</p></li><li><p class="trx-where">Chonburi, Thailand · 2026</p><h3>B300 data hall</h3><p>Every module from 1.6T to 1G, all site-wide InfiniBand and Ethernet switches, and low-loss patch cords, delivered with cabling and system partners.</p></li><li><p class="trx-where">Don Mueang, Thailand · 2026</p><h3>B300 data hall</h3><p>Every module from 1.6T to 1G, all site-wide InfiniBand and Ethernet switches, and low-loss patch cords for error-free long links.</p></li><li><p class="trx-where">Guishan, Taiwan · 2026</p><h3>GB300 data hall</h3><p>1.6T and 800G modules for QM3400 switches and ConnectX-8 network cards, with low-latency cabling.</p></li></ul></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="why-source-through-vocom x6mc4fb"><div class="why-introduction xn9jb0l"><h2 class="x2aydey">Why buy your optics through Vocom</h2></div><div class="sourcing-reason-grid xyelmuz"><div class="build-to-order xwbyhvi fb"><svg class="xmhveue icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"