div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Are your modules compatible with NVIDIA InfiniBand and Ethernet switches?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">They are built to MSA and original-vendor specifications, including heat-dissipating fins, pull-tab color and mechanical dimensions, and they have passed on-site link and interoperability tests in deployed clusters. Send your switch and network card models and we will confirm compatibility part by part.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">What is the difference between OSFP and QSFP-DD?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Both are eight-lane form factors for 400G and 800G. OSFP is slightly larger, with more room to shed heat, and is the form factor used for 1.6T. QSFP-DD is backward compatible with QSFP28 cages and is common on Ethernet switches. The port on your switch or network card decides which one you need.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Why buy transceivers from Vocom instead of the switch vendor?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">You get comparable transmission reliability without the brand premium, with full warranty service, and the modules, patch cords and switches come on one order matched port by port.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Do you supply the patch cords and switches as well?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Yes. Low-loss MPO, MTP and LC patch cords in custom lengths, and InfiniBand and Ethernet switches from the original vendors, supplied with the modules.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Can you install and configure the cluster network?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Yes, through our partners. Specialist cabling contractors handle hot and cold aisle and cable-tray installation, labeling, bend-radius control and fiber loss testing. System configuration partners handle InfiniBand fabric setup, RoCEv2 congestion control tuning and NCCL performance testing.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">How fast can I get a quote for optics?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Within 24 hours. Send the GPU platform, node count, switch and network card models, and any patch cord lengths you already know.</p></div></div><div class="custom-fiber-cta xjri1g2 fb"><p class="xdrf2xf">Need Optics for a Specific Cluster?</p><p class="x7efv2t">Send the GPU platform, node count and switch models. We will return a matched list of modules, patch cords and switches, with a quote within 24 hours.</p><a class="talk-to-a-specifier-button x2urddb" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xvkflym">Request a Quote</p><svg class="xquoydi icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 9.75 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 12)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path></svg></a></div></section><p class="trx-tm">NVIDIA, InfiniBand, ConnectX, BlueField and Quantum are trademarks of their respective owners. Vocom is not affiliated with or endorsed by NVIDIA. Modules are supplied through Vocom's manufacturing partner.</p><div class="simple-footer-2 xzxrxrs footer-slot" data-pagefind-ignore><Footer footerTagline="Your partner for telecommunications and fiber optic supply." title="Quick Links" menu1="VOCOM AI" menu2="Services" menu3="RenOS AI Agents" link2="/vocom-services" link3="/vocom-ai-agents" /></div></div>
